# Lumen problem report logs (install as /system/etc/init/lumen_report.rc; script /system/etc/lumen/lumen_report.sh
# 0755). Shipped in every Lumen image: tools/build/build.py stages both files for every device (COMMON_FILES) and
# refuses a recipe that does not place them.
#
# The report app (apps/core/lumen-report RootLogs) sets sys.lumen.report.req to a new token (the request pattern of
# lumen_hdmirx.rc); this oneshot collects the system log, the crash buffer, the kernel log and three dumpsys summaries,
# scrubbed and size-capped, into /dev/lumen_report (readable only by root and the report app's group), answers in
# sys.lumen.report.done and removes the files once the app set sys.lumen.report.ack to the token (or after 60 s).
# A request that comes while one runs is served by the running script before it exits (init does not start a running
# oneshot twice).
# Labels: the service runs in u:r:su:s0 like every Lumen root helper of these userdebug images (lumen_hdmirx,
# z9x_bootinfo, lumen_dsu_install); sys.lumen.* is system_prop (sys.*); the images run permissive, so the app's read of
# /dev/lumen_report is not refused.
#
# CEC messages in the system log (the report's CEC journal, CecJournal in hdmi.txt): the framework's HdmiLogger prints
# every CEC message it sends or receives ([S]/[R], tag HDMI) only when log.tag.HDMI allows DEBUG, and reads that once
# when system_server loads the class, so it is set here before zygote starts. The message text is built either way;
# the only cost is the log line (about 60 a minute with a soundbar that asks the power status every 2 s).
#
# The persistent log of the last starts (lumen_report.sh keep, the keep section there): from post-fs-data on, as long
# as the unit runs, logcat (main, system, events, crash, radio), the kernel log and periodic dumpsys snapshots go into
# /data/misc/lumen_logs, one folder per start, the newest 6 starts, within a budget of free /data (budget.txt). init
# restarts the service whenever it ends; it goes on in the same start's folder. persist.lumen.logkeep=off stops it.

on early-init
    setprop log.tag.HDMI D

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/misc/lumen_logs 0711 root root
    start lumen_logkeep

on boot
    mkdir /dev/lumen_report 0750 root system

on property:sys.lumen.report.req=* && property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start lumen_report

service lumen_report /system/bin/sh /system/etc/lumen/lumen_report.sh
    user root
    group root system log
    seclabel u:r:su:s0
    oneshot
    disabled

service lumen_logkeep /system/bin/sh /system/etc/lumen/lumen_report.sh keep
    user root
    group root system log
    seclabel u:r:su:s0
    disabled
